WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Gram-negative bacteremia: is 7 days of antibiotics as good as 14?

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.500
The trial randomized 604 patients stable inpatients at 3 centers in Israel and Italy.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.500
Primary outcome at 90 days: 45.8% with 7 days versus 48.3% with 14 days.

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:21.500
Risk difference −2.6%, with the upper confidence limit below the 10% margin. Noninferior.

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.500
Total antibiotic days by day 90: a median of 10 days versus 16 days.

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:33.500
Patients on the short course got back to baseline activity sooner: 2 weeks versus 3 weeks.

7
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:39.500
Seven days was noninferior to 14 days. Clinical Infectious Diseases, 2019. Scroll for the full breakdown.
